{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"genetic disorder\" \"passed down\" parents genes)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_926407421#0_1578719628","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q190","rank":1,"snippet":"RANDOM Term Word in Definition Translations Vocabulary What does genetic disorder mean? Definitions for genetic disorder ge·net·ic dis·or·der Here are all the possible meanings and translations of the word genetic disorder. Princeton's WordNet (0.00 / 0 votes)Rate this definition: genetic disease, genetic disorder, genetic abnormality, genetic defect, congenital disease, inherited disease, inherited disorder, hereditary disease, hereditary condition (noun) a disease or disorder that is inherited genetically Freebase (5.00 / 1 vote)Rate this definition: Genetic disorder A <cover>genetic disorder is an illness caused by one or more abnormalities in the genome, especially a condition that is present from birth. Most genetic disorders are quite rare and affect one person in every several thousands or millions. Genetic disorders are heritable, and are passed down from the parents' genes. </cover>Other defects may be caused by new mutations or changes to the DNA. In such cases, the defect will only be heritable if it occurs in the germ line.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"What does genetic disorder mean?\" , \"url\": \"http://www.definitions.net/definition/genetic%20disorder\" }"}}
