{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"genetic diseases\" \"passed from parents\" children genes)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_666275868#1_1383126917","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q199","rank":1,"snippet":"1175.000000 , \"headings\": \"Is Parkinson’s Hereditary? Is Parkinson’s Hereditary? Overview Is Parkinson’s hereditary? Genes Can Parkinson’s be passed from parent to child? Risk factors Prevention When to see a doctor The takeaway \" , \"segment\": \"Parkinson’s disease is a neurodegenerative disorder that affects the nervous system. It causes tremors, shaking, slow movement, balance problems, and stiffness. Parkinson’s disease usually affects people who are older. Is Parkinson’s hereditary? Hereditary diseases are those that are <cover>passed from parents to their children through their genes. A genetic disease can be hereditary or not. Some genetic diseases </cover>are caused by random mutations that aren’t inherited from the parents. Studies show that some cases of Parkinson’s disease are caused by genetic mutations. Hereditary causes of this disease are rare. Only 15 percent of those who have Parkinson’s disease have a family history of it.\" , \"start_char\": 482.000000 , \"title\": \"Is Parkinson’s Hereditary? The Role of Genetics in Parkinson’s Disease\" , \"url\": \"https://www.healthline.com/health/"}}
