{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_666275868#1_1383126917","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage directly defines hereditary diseases as diseases passed from parents to children through genes and distinguishes hereditary genetic disease from non-inherited genetic mutations. However, the document is primarily about Parkinson’s disease rather than dedicated to the general mechanism of hereditary disease transmission.","learned":"Hereditary diseases are passed from parents to children through genes; some genetic diseases arise from random mutations and are not inherited."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q199","reason":"This query produced direct definitional evidence, so subsequent results may include broader pages about genetic diseases and inheritance rather than disease-specific articles."}}
