{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"inherited disease\" \"passed down\" families genes)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1740841166#0_3567325760","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q200","rank":1,"snippet":"\"Alport Syndrome Alport Syndrome What is Alport syndrome? What causes Alport syndrome? What are the genetic types of Alport syndrome? What are the signs and symptoms of Alport syndrome? How is Alport syndrome diagnosed? How is Alport syndrome treated? Where can I find more information? \" , \"segment\": \"Alport Syndrome | National Kidney Foundation Alport Syndrome What is Alport syndrome? Alport syndrome is a disease that damages the tiny blood vessels in your kidneys. It can lead to kidney disease and kidney failure. It can also cause hearing loss and problems within the eyes. Alport syndrome causes damage to your kidneys by attacking the glomeruli. Glomeruli are the tiny filtering units inside your kidneys. What causes Alport syndrome? Alport syndrome is an <cover>inherited disease, which means it is passed down through families. It is caused by changes in your genes (</cover>mutations) to a protein called collagen. Collagen is important to the normal structure and function of the kidneys.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Alport Syndrome | National Kidney Foundation\" , \"url\": \"https://www.kidney.org/atoz/content/Alport\" }"}}
