{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"genetic disorders are inherited\" parents genes)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1299898824#0_2376701312","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q207","rank":1,"snippet":"07_1299898824#0_2376701312\" , \"end_char\": 641.000000 , \"headings\": \"Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited\" , \"segment\": \"Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited - Mayo Clinic Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited Previous Next 1 of 6 Your genes, chromosomes and DNA Your body is made up of trillions of cells. Each cell has a core structure (nucleus) that contains your chromosomes. Each chromosome is made up of tightly coiled strands of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA). Genes are segments of DNA that determine specific traits, such as eye or hair color. You have more than 20,000 <cover>genes. You have two copies of each gene — one inherited from each of your parents. A variant is a change in your DNA.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited - </cover>Mayo Clinic\" , \"url\": \"http://www.mayoclinic.org/tests-procedures/genetic-testing/multimedia/genetic-disorders/sls-20076216\" }"}}
