{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1299898824#0_2376701312","relevance":3,"reason":"The Mayo Clinic slideshow is explicitly dedicated to how genetic disorders are inherited and directly explains the basis of inheritance: genes are DNA segments on chromosomes, people have two copies of each gene, one inherited from each parent, and DNA variants can underlie disorders.","learned":"Genetic disorders are passed through inherited DNA: genes are segments of DNA on chromosomes, and each person inherits one copy of each gene from each parent; variants are DNA changes."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q207","reason":"This query found a highly authoritative, dedicated source on how genetic disorders are inherited; the remaining slideshow segments are likely to explain inheritance patterns and provide more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q207"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1299898824#1_2376702365","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q207","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1299898824#1_2376702365\" , \"end_char\": 993.000000 , \"headings\": \"Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited Slide show: How <cover>genetic disorders are inherited\" , \"segment\": \"Each chromosome is made up of tightly coiled strands of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA). Genes are segments of DNA that determine specific traits, such as eye or hair color. You have more than 20,000 genes. You have two copies of each gene — one inherited from each of your parents. </cover>A variant is a change in your DNA. Some variants are benign — they're not associated with health problems. Other variants are pathogenic — they're associated with a genetic or health condition. Pathogenic variants are sometimes called mutations. Many types of pathogenic variants cause a change in or damage to a gene. These abnormal genes (gene mutations) can be inherited or acquired.\" , \"start_char\": 327.000000 , \"title\": \"Slide show: How genetic disorders are inherited - Mayo Clinic\" , \"url\": \"http://www.mayoclinic.org/"}}
