{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_1299898824#1_2376702365","relevance":3,"reason":"This Mayo Clinic slideshow segment is dedicated to how genetic disorders are inherited and directly explains that genes are DNA segments on chromosomes, people inherit one copy of each gene from each parent, and pathogenic variants/mutations can be inherited or acquired.","learned":"Genetic disorders can be inherited through pathogenic DNA variants in genes; each person inherits gene copies from both parents, and some abnormal genes are inherited while others are acquired."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q207","reason":"The Mayo Clinic slideshow is highly relevant and likely has additional segments explaining dominant, recessive, and sex-linked inheritance patterns, so continue through this query."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q207"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1518908315#8_3080849478","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q207","rank":3,"snippet":"Colorblindness Risk Factors Other Causes A Word From Verywell \" , \"segment\": \"Unlike other forms of color vision deficiency, it can also cause vision issues such as light sensitivity, limited visual acuity, farsightedness, and nearsightedness. It’s inherited via an autosomal recessive pattern. Both <cover>parents have to have the recessive gene to pass it down, which is why it’s so rare. There are also some cases of achromatopsia where the cause is unknown. Only 1 in 30,000 people worldwide have this condition. 5 ﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿﻿ Risk Factors You’re more likely to be colorblind if: Someone in your family is colorblind You have an eye disease You take medications with colorblindness as a side effect You have a brain or nervous system disease like multiple sclerosis (MS) You are White Understanding How Genetic Disorders Are Inherited Other Causes Color vision deficiency that isn’t caused by genes </cover>is called an acquired vision deficiency. Potential non-genetic causes of color blindness include: Certain drugs Chemical exposure Eye disorders Damage to the optic nerve Damage to areas of the brain that are responsible for visual processing Color vision can also diminish as you get older. In cases of "}}
