{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"genetic disorder runs in my family\" children condition inherited)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1156301429#11_2541801068","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q212","rank":1,"snippet":"in my family, what are the chances that my children will have the condition? Topics in the Inheriting Genetic Conditions chapter \" , \"segment\": \"Estimating the chance of developing or passing on a genetic disorder can be complex. Genetics professionals can help people understand these chances and help them make informed decisions about their health. Topics in the Inheriting Genetic Conditions chapter Collapse Section What does it mean if a disorder seems to run in my family? Why is it important to know my family health history? What are the different ways a genetic <cover>condition can be inherited? If a genetic disorder runs in my family, what are the chances that my children </cover>will have the condition? What are reduced penetrance and variable expressivity? What do geneticists mean by anticipation? What are genomic imprinting and uniparental disomy? Are chromosomal disorders inherited?\" , \"start_char\": 6530.000000 , \"title\": \"If a genetic disorder runs in my family, what are the chances that my children will have the condition?: MedlinePlus Genetics\" , \"url\": \"https://ghr.nlm.nih.gov/primer/inheritance/riskassessment\" }"}}
