{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1613101379#8_3389434174","relevance":3,"reason":"The Britannica human genetic disease page is dedicated to inherited genetic disease mechanisms and the snippet directly supports how disease can be passed by inheritance, including a child inheriting mutant gene copies from a parent and multifactorial inherited disorders.","learned":"Inherited genetic disease can result when children receive mutant gene copies from parents; rare mechanisms such as uniparental disomy can allow a child to inherit two mutant copies from one carrier parent, and multifactorial inheritance is another class of inherited disorders."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q216","reason":"This query is producing broad, direct explanations of genetic disorders and inherited mutations from authoritative sources, so continue to collect additional grade-3 evidence."}}
