{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1613101379#9_3389436714","relevance":3,"reason":"This Britannica human genetic disease segment directly explains inherited disease mechanisms: a child can inherit mutant gene copies from a carrier parent, and multifactorial genetic disorders involve multiple genes often acting with environmental factors. It is near-duplicate evidence from the same Britannica page but still directly supports hereditary disease transmission.","learned":"Repeated Britannica evidence: hereditary disorders can occur when children inherit mutant gene copies from parents; multifactorial inherited disorders involve multiple genes and sometimes environmental factors."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q216","reason":"The current query has produced several broad, direct sources about genetic disorders caused by inherited mutations; continue to see if more ranked results provide additional grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q216"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_428726263#3_1027578661","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q216","rank":5,"snippet":"Inheritest results Understand Costs About your results Genetic counseling Reference \" , \"segment\": \"desire to be empowered with information about your genetic risks for family planning purposes concerns regarding inherited disorders an increased risk of being a carrier of an inherited disorder due to ethnic background a family history of a specific inherited disorder Genetic disorders may be <cover>caused by a change in a gene. This change is called a mutation. Most genetic disorders are inherited through what is referred to as autosomal recessive inheritance. Every person has two copies of each gene, one inherited from each parent. With autosomal recessive inheritance, a carrier is a person who has one normal copy of a gene and one mutated copy. Having one normal gene is often enough to prevent the disorder. When both parents </cover>are carriers of the same mutation, there is a chance that each parent will pass this mutation on to their baby. If the baby inherits two copies of the mutated gene, the baby will have the disorder ( prenatal diagnosis can be performed to determine whether or not the fetus is affected). (NOTE: In addition to autosomal recessive diseases, some genes require only the "}}
